problem:
Problem description
- There are $$N$$ factories indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{F}$$ and $$N$$ locations indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{L}$$, with $$|\mathcal{F}| = |\mathcal{L}| = N$$.
- For each ordered factory pair $$\left(i,j\right)$$, the parameter $$d_{ij}$$ denotes the transportation volume between factories $$i$$ and $$j$$.
- For each ordered location pair $$\left(p,q\right)$$, the parameter $$c_{pq}$$ denotes the unit transportation cost from location $$p$$ to location $$q$$.
- The planning goal is to assign factories to locations so that the total transportation cost induced by all factory-to-factory volumes, after the assignment of factories to locations, is minimized.
- The assignment must be one-to-one: each factory must be placed at exactly one location, and each location must be used by exactly one factory.
- The decision must be integral, so the assignment choices are binary.
- A solution is represented by:
  - a binary assignment matrix $$X = \left[x_{ip}\right]$$, where $$x_{ip} = 1$$ if factory $$i$$ is assigned to location $$p$$, and $$x_{ip} = 0$$ otherwise;
  - optionally, an equivalent assignment vector $$\pi$$, where $$\pi_i$$ is the location assigned to factory $$i$$;
  - the resulting total transportation cost value.

Input Format
{
  "N": "integer; the common number of factories and locations, $$|\mathcal{F}| = |\mathcal{L}| = N$$",
  "D": {
    "shape": "$$N \\times N$$",
    "type": "matrix of nonnegative values",
    "meaning": "$$D = \\left[d_{ij}\\right]$$, where $$d_{ij}$$ is the transportation volume between factories $$i$$ and $$j$$"
  },
  "C": {
    "shape": "$$N \\times N$$",
    "type": "matrix of nonnegative values",
    "meaning": "$$C = \\left[c_{pq}\\right]$$, where $$c_{pq}$$ is the unit transportation cost from location $$p$$ to location $$q$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "assignment_matrix": {
    "shape": "$$N \\times N$$",
    "type": "binary matrix",
    "meaning": "$$X = \\left[x_{ip}\\right]$$, where $$x_{ip} = 1$$ if factory $$i$$ is assigned to location $$p$$"
  },
  "assignment_vector": {
    "shape": "$$N$$",
    "type": "integer vector",
    "meaning": "$$\\pi_i$$ is the location assigned to factory $$i$$"
  },
  "total_transportation_cost": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "type": "nonnegative value",
    "meaning": "the minimized total cost achieved by the assignment"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "N": 2,
  "D": [
    [10, 20],
    [30, 40]
  ],
  "C": [
    [5, 8],
    [6, 7]
  ]
}
